      "field": "material_initial_state; baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed HIP schedule is 900–1000 °C for 2–4 hours at approximately 100–150 MPa, followed by controlled slow cooling.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "HIP will reduce internal porosity in the target alloy through high-pressure, high-temperature densification.",
      "field": "hypothesis; structural_mediator; mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "HIP will heal microcracks in the target alloy through high-temperature diffusion under pressure.",
      "field": "hypothesis; structural_mediator; mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "HIP will refine or make the target alloy's microstructure more uniform.",
      "field": "structural_mediator; mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The HIP treatment will preserve the crystallographic phases and phase boundaries responsible for the caloric response.",
      "field": "structural_mediator; mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7512535::web::030::5_summary"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Maintaining those crystallographic phases will maintain the alloy's large caloric response.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Defect elimination and microstructural homogenization will significantly increase compressive strength.",
      "field": "hypothesis; mechanism; predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "HIP treatment will markedly reduce cracking relative to the as-cast alloy.",
      "field": "hypothesis; predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The HIP-treated alloy is targeted to exceed approximately 150–200 MPa in compressive strength.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "HIP will cause minimal to no loss in isothermal entropy change or adiabatic temperature change.",
      "field": "hypothesis; predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The HIP-treated alloy will retain improved integrity during cyclic magnetic-field and pressure-field operation.",
      "field": "conditions; boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention is expected to remain effective during temperature cycling and compressive loading typical of magnetocaloric applications.",
      "field": "conditions; boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The HIP-treated material is expected to perform effectively at temperatures up to around 1000 °C.",
